.env.local
# Any variant — .env.local.dev, .env.local.prod, backups while switching
# projects. The bare name above does not cover a suffixed copy, and a
# credentials file one character away from being committed is not worth the
# risk.
.env.local*
.env*.local
node_modules/
npm-debug.log*

# Dev-server output. Eleven of these were tracked, and a running dev server
# rewrites them constantly -- so every checkout and merge tripped over "local
# changes would be overwritten", which is what forced a branch-ref push instead
# of a normal merge. Machine-local process output, no value in history.
# Covers npm-debug.log* above too; that line is kept because it is conventional.
*.log

# Review reports generated from live data. They quote real customer messages in
# full — names, phone numbers, order references — which is the whole reason they
# are useful and the whole reason they must not be committed.
situation-matches.html
*-review.html
